 "entry": "attendance.models.Session.to_api",
 "format": 1,
 "notes": ["The input is the fields of the object. The generator makes the model from them and calls the entry point. A route of attendance.api then writes the result.","A time in args is in the ISO 8601 form of Python. The generator reads it with datetime.fromisoformat.","output is the exact bytes that the Python code writes.","args.state, args.turns_running and args.writer are the three arguments of the entry point. Each other field of args is a field of the Session.","The labels of a session have free form. Every object of free form inside args has its keys in sorted order. A vector file sorts keys, and the Python code keeps the order that it is given."],
 "surface": "session.answer.session",
